  "description": "\u201cTo place at a given point (as an extremity) a straight line equal to a given straight line.\u201d\n\u2014 Euclid's Elements, BOOK I \u2022 PROP. 2 (G.20)\n\n00:00 1 \u00b7 GIVEN: point A and segment BC\n00:06 2 \u00b7 GOAL: segment AL = BC at point A\n00:13 3 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: segment AB\n00:16 4 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: equilateral triangle DAB\n00:20 5 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: extend DA to E and DB to F\n00:23 6 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: circle ( B C )\n00:27 7 \u00b7 INTERSECT: intersection point G\n00:30 8 \u00b7 CONSTRUCT: circle ( D G )\n00:34 9 \u00b7 INTERSECT: intersection point L\n00:36 10 \u00b7 ASSERT: BC = BG\n00:43 11 \u00b7 ASSERT: DL = DG\n00:50 12 \u00b7 ASSERT: AL = BG\n00:59 13 \u00b7 \u2234: AL = BC at point A\n\nGEOMETOR \u2022 G.20 \u2022 v4",
